;;; (7) THEOREM 4.13 (Casorati-Weierstrass): f holomorphic on u \ {a} with an essential singularity at a takes, on
;;;     every punctured ball about a, values arbitrarily close to every w.  Otherwise |f - w| >= eps near a, so
;;;     g = 1/(f - w) is bounded there, removable (4.3) with extension G; G = (z - a)^m H (zero-order-exists, G is
;;;     non-zero off a), and f = w + 1/G = (1/(z - a))^m (w (z - a)^m + 1/H) is meromorphic at a: a removable
;;;     singularity or a pole (meromorphic-point-cases), not essential.
